      {"text":"// \"true\", \"false\" and \"nil\" are predeclared identifiers Go lets a program redeclare. Where they name something", "contentText":" \"true\", \"false\" and \"nil\" are predeclared identifiers Go lets a program redeclare. Where they name something", "range":"3:0::111", "contentRange": "3:2::111"},
      {"text":"// they are identifiers, and so is a read of a redeclared name; only a read of the predeclared value is a literal.", "contentText":" they are identifiers, and so is a read of a redeclared name; only a read of the predeclared value is a literal.", "range":"4:0::114", "contentRange": "4:2::114"},
      {"text":"// They live in their own file: declaring them at package scope would change the meaning of every case sharing it.", "contentText":" They live in their own file: declaring them at package scope would change the meaning of every case sharing it.", "range":"5:0::114", "contentRange": "5:2::114"},
